WEBVTT

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:20.660
There you are!

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:24.460
Gavin-senpai!

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:25.970
I told you.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:29.170
I would never hurt you.

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:38.450
You're not injured?

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:40.760
Lucien... What was that?

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:43.600
I was going to tell you one day.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.100
I'm an Evolver, too.

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:49.690
Although I didn't manage to be of much use.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:53.110
I'm glad you're safe.

00:00:53.390 --> 00:00:55.450
<i>So many things were happening at once,</i>

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:58.350
<i>trying to change my everyday 
life in tremendous ways.</i>

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:00.520
<i>Were they all coincidences,</i>

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:04.110
<i>or had they always been fated to happen?</i>

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:15.470
"It takes all the running you can do, 
to keep in the same place."

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:15.470
~The Red Queen Hypothesis~

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:21.610
<i>In this world, there exist 
unique powers known as "Evol,"</i>

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:23.850
<i>which are possessed by a very few.</i>

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:28.270
<i>Among them, some chose to fight 
their fate, to fight the world.</i>

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:30.920
<i>This is the story of these young "Evolvers."</i>

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:51.020
<b>Mr. Love: Queen's Choice</b>

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:54.400
"The Key in the Darkness"

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:57.440
Hey, President! Did you see this?

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:00.400
Miracle Entertainment

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:01.230
The response to the episode Kiro did 
about Souvenir has been incredible!

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.870
I recommend the pudding♪ 
It's like it comes alive in your mouth♪ 
#MiracleFinder! #Souvenir #kiro

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:02.870
Th-Three million?!

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:05.390
This is it for us!

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:08.400
We're gonna ride this momentum, 
make a bunch of new episodes,

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.940
and get a ton of new viewers!

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:12.840
Exactly!

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:15.210
But there is no need to fret any longer,

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:19.390
because I, overflowing with brilliance 
and good taste, have arrived.

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:20.170
Right?

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:21.860
Who are you?

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:23.040
Oh!

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:24.960
You're... Minor?

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:25.760
Hey!

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:28.190
<i>Minor and I were in the 
same class in high school,</i>

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:32.270
<i>and he was the only one in the whole 
school who seemed close to Gavin-senpai.</i>

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:34.920
Wh-Why are you here?

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:36.060
Well, you know.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:39.940
Lately, I've been hearing that 
<i>Miracle Finder</i> is making some waves.

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:44.160
And I thought, since we used to be in 
the same class, I should come help you out.

00:03:44.840 --> 00:03:47.570
In other words... you can't find a job.

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:50.240
You mean he's looking for a job here?

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:52.190
What? You want me to work 
with someone like him?

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:53.080
No way!

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:54.250
W-Wait a sec!

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:57.160
I didn't come empty-handed.

00:03:57.160 --> 00:04:00.510
I brought you some great material 
that could make for a good show.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:02.360
Great material?

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:05.420
Have you heard the name "Key" before?

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:07.720
Key? You mean the famous hacker?

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:09.470
Of course we've heard of him.

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:12.710
<i>Key is a legendary hacker
who earned instant notoriety</i>

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:15.590
<i>after an incident seventeen years ago.</i>

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:18.650
<i>He infiltrated the servers of a 
certain genetic research facility</i>

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:21.150
<i>and published all their research 
findings on the internet.</i>

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:24.860
<i>Concerned by the data, my father 
decided to do a report on the incident,</i>

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:26.480
<i>and the fact that they had</i>

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:30.280
<i>kidnapped people for use in 
illegal experimentation was exposed.</i>

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:31.670
<i>The program where he reported this</i>

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:34.290
<i>would eventually become the origin 
of the show </i>Miracle Finder<i>.</i>

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:39.310
<i>However, after that incident, 
Key completely disappeared.</i>

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:42.360
Yes, that Key!

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:45.250
He reappeared about a year ago!

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:47.340
Fixed Income 
Fees Received 
Commission Received 

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:46.840
Just like seventeen years ago,

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:50.310
he's going around exposing companies' 
wrongdoings and malicious hackers' crimes.

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:54.760
Everyone underground is talking about
"the return of the righteous hacker"!

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:56.650
Oh, I know about that.

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:57.470
Huh?!

00:04:57.470 --> 00:04:59.650
It made regular internet news, too.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:02.010
"Underground," huh?

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:05.400
That said, the material itself isn't bad.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:06.660
A hacker for justice...

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:10.300
But we're talking about someone 
whose identity is unknown.

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:13.680
It might be hard if we can't 
manage a single interview.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:16.910
Huh? Is this, like, going bad?

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:18.790
What about my job?

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:22.460
Well, having more help won't hurt.

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:24.540
For now, we'll hire you as an apprentice.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:25.050
What?

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.360
For real? Thanks!

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:29.420
My name is Minor.

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:32.470
I'll work as hard as you need me to, 
so let me know what to do!

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:39.370
<i>The hacker that lead to Papa 
starting </i>Miracle Finder<i>...</i>

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:43.820
Inbox

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:43.820
To: Kenkoku-niisan 

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:46.270
Kenkoku-niisan?

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:47.280
Who is that?

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:51.100
It's hosted by Key?!

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:58.030
Kenkoku-niisan, 
I'm sending you that invitation. 
I think I contacted you about this before,
 but next Friday, Key is hosting 
a top-class seminar, 
and I was hoping you'd come. 
Details are in the data I've attached. 
See you there.

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:53.610
<i>I see.</i>

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:57.120
<i>Key is holding a meet-up 
for hackers to share their skills.</i>

00:05:57.490 --> 00:06:01.820
<i>Someone who's participating is trying to 
send an invitation to this "Kenkoku-niisan,"</i>

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:04.380
<i>but it came to me by accident.</i>

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:07.720
Do coincidences like this really happen?

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:11.160
<i>But... if I go, I might be able to meet Key.</i>

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:23.070
That being said... 
is this really the right place?

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:28.990
This is where...

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:45.280
It's been a while...

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:47.850
Like this, right?

00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:48.990
That'll start it up.

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:49.880
Really?

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:52.550
You should do it.

00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:54.580
We should make an app.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:55.690
Wow...

00:06:55.690 --> 00:06:58.290
Are all these people really hackers?

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:00.660
Hey. Are you here for this, too?

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:04.650
Uh, yes! I'm Kenkoku-niisan.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:07.030
Wh-What'd you say?!

00:07:07.310 --> 00:07:10.280
Wait, so Kenkoku-niisan is actually a girl?!

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:14.440
I love your spiky style! 
It's why I made my hair like this!

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:16.010
I wanna hear everything!

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:19.500
<i>H-Huh? What kind of person 
is this "Kenkoku-niisan"?</i>

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:22.670
Oh, there you are! 
I've been looking for you!

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:23.880
Huh? What?

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:25.590
W-Wait!

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:26.670
Let go!

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:30.920
It's all right. It's just me.

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:32.630
K... Ki—

00:07:34.150 --> 00:07:37.100
Something like this happened before, 
didn't it, Potato Chip Princess?

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:40.250
Wh-Why are you here?

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:41.850
Do you know what this place is?

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:43.190
Of course.

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:46.600
But what about you? Why the getup?

00:07:47.350 --> 00:07:48.740
Does it look weird?

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:51.660
I tried to make it look hacker-ish...

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:52.650
See?

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:55.370
Well, that aside...

00:07:55.710 --> 00:07:57.580
<i>H-He just brushed it off.</i>

00:07:57.890 --> 00:08:01.760
Are you saying that behind your 
producer persona, you're really a hacker?

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:03.680
No, not at all!

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:06.270
We're currently planning 
an episode featuring Key,

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:07.810
and I'm here to get info—

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:18.890
Hey!

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:19.730
Are you okay?

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:20.710
What was that?

00:08:20.710 --> 00:08:22.060
Wh-What?

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:23.210
What is this?

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:26.020
Upon the loathsome hackers, I bestow a gift. 
A gift known as "death"—

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:26.010
What's going on?

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:39.160
Is that...

00:08:39.630 --> 00:08:40.570
What is this?

00:08:40.570 --> 00:08:41.920
This has gotta be a joke!

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:43.890
Are you stupid? You saw what just happened!

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:45.720
I ain't hanging around for this crap.

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:48.340
If the elevator doesn't work, 
there's the emergency stairs.

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:50.180
Damn it!

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:51.710
The doors are welded shut!

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:54.630
Everyone, calm down!

00:08:55.230 --> 00:08:57.480
During a crisis is when we 
most need to stay rational!

00:08:57.880 --> 00:09:00.350
The more we panic, the more
 we play into their hands!

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:04.060
Don't worry! There must be a way 
for us to get out of this!

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:06.380
Th-That's right.

00:09:06.380 --> 00:09:07.560
It's just like he says.

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:09.420
Let's go, everyone! Get up!

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:09.420
We're getting out of here!

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:11.190
Let's look for another way outside!

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:12.520
<i>Amazing...</i>

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:15.320
<i>The panic quieted down like magic.</i>

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:18.120
From what I can tell,

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:21.110
the bomb is likely operated via wireless remote.

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:25.710
If we go through the communication module 
into the program used for the detonator

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:27.920
and enter a cancel command, it should stop.

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:47.060
<i>Keep fighting, everyone!</i>

00:09:53.390 --> 00:09:54.180
No good!

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:55.800
Is there any other way through?

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:58.360
Don't worry! Leave it to me.

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:09.140
Got it!

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:20.830
<i>Please... Stop!</i>

00:10:25.430 --> 00:10:26.270
<i>Please!</i>

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:50.000
Just barely made it...

00:10:55.140 --> 00:10:56.600
Yes!

00:10:56.600 --> 00:10:57.890
We're saved!

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:02.500
Hey! It's open!

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:03.710
We can get out!

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:04.890
I'm beat!

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:07.650
Thank you! We owe it all to you.

00:11:07.650 --> 00:11:09.690
I didn't do it alone.

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:14.250
Besides, helping those in need 
is what a hero of justice does!

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:21.460
Potato Chip Princess!

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:40.590
Are you hurt?

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:42.150
Kiro...

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:45.140
I-I'm so sorry!

00:11:45.690 --> 00:11:48.300
Looks like we got caught in a pitfall trap.

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:49.600
A pitfall?

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:52.370
Is this Key's doing, too?

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:53.630
No.

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:56.040
He's not responsible for this pitfall,

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:57.590
nor for the bomb earlier.

00:11:58.620 --> 00:12:00.450
How are you so sure?

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:01.490
Well, because...

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:03.030
I'm Key.

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:07.530
What?

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:12.040
The true identity of Key is me, 
Potato Chip Princess.

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:17.040
<b>Mr. Love: Queen's Choice</b>

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:22.050
<b>Mr. Love: Queen's Choice</b>

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:25.470
K-Kiro... you're Key?

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:27.730
That's right! I'm Key.

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:28.760
Surprised?

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:33.220
Well, to be accurate, 
I'm the second generation.

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:35.290
Second generation?

00:12:35.290 --> 00:12:36.090
Yup.

00:12:36.090 --> 00:12:39.140
The Key from seventeen 
years ago was my master.

00:12:39.140 --> 00:12:42.780
But after my master disappeared, 
I took on his name.

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:45.530
Then all the stuff that's 
been happening lately...

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:47.200
It was all my handiwork.

00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:50.280
Then, Kiro, you really are...

00:12:50.280 --> 00:12:53.980
B-But you're an idol. Why would you...

00:12:54.340 --> 00:12:56.220
Before I explain that,

00:12:56.220 --> 00:12:58.340
we should probably get out of here.

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:03.260
When I was hacking earlier, I got a 
diagram of the building from the server.

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:05.680
This is where we are.

00:13:06.030 --> 00:13:08.140
Let's head for this control room first.

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:11.770
The building's security is managed from there,

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:14.030
so if we disable it, 
we'll be able to leave safely.

00:13:14.030 --> 00:13:15.070
Got it?

00:13:15.070 --> 00:13:16.230
Y-Yeah.

00:13:22.840 --> 00:13:26.930
Up to now, I've exposed lots 
of different crimes as Key.

00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:28.880
Just like a hero of justice.

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:31.030
My master taught me.

00:13:31.030 --> 00:13:33.440
"We live in the darkness 
and protect the light.

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:35.040
That's who Key is," he said.

00:13:35.850 --> 00:13:39.130
And I have a special power 
just for that purpose.

00:13:39.570 --> 00:13:42.210
Could it be... an Evol?

00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:44.290
You know about that?

00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:46.550
That's right. I'm an Evolver.

00:13:47.210 --> 00:13:49.400
I have a special sort of charm.

00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:52.660
One look at me and people are captivated, 
no matter who they are.

00:13:52.960 --> 00:13:56.230
It's superhero Key's secret weapon!

00:13:56.760 --> 00:13:58.940
Some people who think of me as a nuisance

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:01.860
used Key's name to try to draw me out.

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:07.740
<b>Seminar Announcement 

00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:04.480
So you came knowing it was a trap?

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:05.640
That's right.

00:14:05.640 --> 00:14:07.740
I wanted to find out more about them.

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:11.690
But... because of that, I ended up 
getting you mixed up in this.

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:14.370
I'm really... really sorry.

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:16.210
D-Don't be!

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:19.080
I came out to a place like this 
of my own volition, after all.

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:21.460
There's no reason for you to feel bad about it!

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:26.240
Don't worry. I promise I'll get 
you out of here in one piece.

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:27.440
I promise.

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:30.430
Are you okay, Potato Chip Princess?

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:31.780
Yeah!

00:14:31.780 --> 00:14:34.350
I'm clueless about hacker skills and stuff,

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:37.540
but I won't slow you down. Don't worry!

00:14:53.050 --> 00:14:54.800
I-I'm sorry!

00:14:55.820 --> 00:14:57.500
Kiro! Your arm!

00:14:59.990 --> 00:15:01.910
You'll have to make do with this for now.

00:15:01.910 --> 00:15:04.980
It's fine! It's not a bad injury.

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:06.530
<i>It's my fault...</i>

00:15:06.530 --> 00:15:09.260
<i>And right after I said 
I wouldn't slow him down...</i>

00:15:09.610 --> 00:15:11.730
Potato Chip Princess, open your mouth.

00:15:11.730 --> 00:15:12.540
Huh?

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:16.350
It's magic candy that makes you feel better.

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:18.670
Green apple flavor?

00:15:18.670 --> 00:15:20.550
It's my favorite flavor.

00:15:20.550 --> 00:15:22.740
Yeah. It's delicious!

00:15:22.740 --> 00:15:24.790
Don't tell my manager, okay?

00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:27.560
He's really fussy when it comes to sweets.

00:15:27.560 --> 00:15:29.430
It's our secret.

00:15:29.840 --> 00:15:31.360
Thank you, Kiro.

00:15:33.880 --> 00:15:35.830
This is the control room.

00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:38.660
Wait just a sec. I'll be done in a flash.

00:15:41.340 --> 00:15:42.370
All that's left is...

00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:46.960
Okay! I disabled it!

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:49.560
And now I'll get info on them, too.

00:15:56.380 --> 00:15:58.370
Wh-What's going on?

00:15:58.370 --> 00:16:00.850
All the oxygen is being drawn out.

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:03.070
This isn't right...

00:16:03.070 --> 00:16:06.040
I should have full control 
over the system, so why...

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:08.320
A password?

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:11.490
There's no point in overthinking.

00:16:17.690 --> 00:16:19.140
I can't breathe...

00:16:19.140 --> 00:16:20.280
Are you okay?

00:16:20.280 --> 00:16:21.370
Y-Yeah.

00:16:22.470 --> 00:16:25.280
<i>I've... seen this before, somewhere...</i>

00:16:29.530 --> 00:16:32.170
<i>Could that have been...</i>

00:16:33.410 --> 00:16:35.040
That didn't work, either?

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:38.960
368...

00:16:38.960 --> 00:16:39.760
What?

00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:43.020
Can you think of anything 
that starts with those numbers?

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:58.530
We're saved.

00:16:58.530 --> 00:17:00.090
How did you know?

00:17:00.090 --> 00:17:03.520
I don't know if you'll believe me or not,

00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:04.870
but I saw it in a dream.

00:17:05.240 --> 00:17:07.020
Does that mean—

00:17:07.770 --> 00:17:09.510
Looks like the download is done.

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:12.120
This is... a report?

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:16.100
Papa?

00:17:16.540 --> 00:17:21.160
"The target learned the secret of 
the organization and Evolvers, and so...

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:22.220
was eliminated."

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:40.930
It's all right.

00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:45.090
You're all right. I'm here with you.

00:17:49.800 --> 00:17:52.320
<i>So all this time, it wasn't me they were after.</i>

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:55.480
<i>It was all to show her this?</i>

00:18:03.240 --> 00:18:06.860
<i>That day... you gave me strength.</i>

00:18:08.170 --> 00:18:11.110
<i>In the darkness, we protect the light.</i>

00:18:11.990 --> 00:18:14.230
I will protect you, no matter what,

00:18:14.750 --> 00:18:17.750
with this strength you gave me.

00:18:30.620 --> 00:18:31.570
Huh?

00:18:31.990 --> 00:18:34.660
How... did I...

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:37.470
A present for you 
-KIRO

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:41.540
I see. Kiro carried me here.

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:47.890
Papa was targeted by Black Swan and...

00:18:48.640 --> 00:18:50.870
<b>The target learned the secret of the organization 
and Evolvers, and so was eliminated.</b>

00:18:56.520 --> 00:18:59.550
I feel like I was on the verge of
 remembering something back there.

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:02.910
Lucien

00:19:04.980 --> 00:19:06.360
<i>Lucien?</i>

00:19:06.360 --> 00:19:09.820
It seemed like you were out 
awfully late, so I was worried...

00:19:09.820 --> 00:19:12.070
But I should probably call back another time.

00:19:12.070 --> 00:19:14.160
<i>No, it's all right.</i>

00:19:14.770 --> 00:19:17.950
If you don't mind, would you
 talk to me a little?

00:19:17.950 --> 00:19:20.600
The way I am now, I don't 
think I'll be able to sleep.

00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:21.950
<i>Really?</i>

00:19:21.950 --> 00:19:25.860
<i>Then how about a recently 
published paper on psychology?</i>

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:30.090
<i>When I lectured on it at the university, 
several people looked quite sleepy.</i>

00:19:30.090 --> 00:19:32.240
Something a little simpler, if you could.

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:34.560
<i>All right.</i>

00:19:34.930 --> 00:19:38.550
Then I'll tell you my favorite fairy tale.

00:19:40.120 --> 00:19:44.610
Once upon a time, a solitary 
painter lived in a castle.

00:19:45.390 --> 00:19:48.800
He used only black and white, 
just those two colors.

00:19:49.470 --> 00:19:52.380
To him, the world looked 
as though those two colors

00:19:52.380 --> 00:19:55.080
were the only ones that existed.

00:19:55.660 --> 00:20:00.120
One day, an incredibly beautiful 
butterfly appeared before him.

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:05.850
The butterfly's wings were rich with 
vivid colors he'd never seen before.

00:20:06.570 --> 00:20:11.350
The painter was enchanted by the butterfly, 
and painted it day after day.

00:20:12.380 --> 00:20:17.400
But the painter began to worry that 
the butterfly might disappear one day.

00:20:18.310 --> 00:20:20.400
That's when he thought...

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:23.020
If he were able to capture the butterfly,

00:20:23.020 --> 00:20:25.990
he might be able to keep it with him always.

00:20:26.860 --> 00:20:30.910
The painter must have been 
very afraid to lose the butterfly.

00:20:32.490 --> 00:20:36.070
<i>But if it were me, I might 
have chosen a different way.</i>

00:20:36.510 --> 00:20:37.460
Why?

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:41.040
Because I'm sure the butterfly 
also didn't want to lose

00:20:41.040 --> 00:20:43.850
its sky, or the freedom 
to spread its wings.

00:20:44.390 --> 00:20:48.260
That's why instead of capturing it, 
I would chase after it.

00:20:48.820 --> 00:20:51.050
<i>Rather than look away from 
a future where it's lost to me,</i>

00:20:51.050 --> 00:20:52.840
<i>I'd want to keep moving forward.</i>

00:20:53.280 --> 00:20:58.150
<i>Otherwise, I feel like I'll never 
obtain what is truly precious.</i>

00:21:04.270 --> 00:21:06.720
Rather than look away from 
a future where it's lost to you,

00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:09.760
you'd keep moving forward...

00:21:10.670 --> 00:21:13.280
I knew you would say that.

00:22:48.240 --> 00:22:51.070
One more step and the Queen will awaken.

00:22:51.760 --> 00:22:53.640
Every time life is faced with a crisis,

00:22:53.640 --> 00:22:56.790
the Queen's genes progress 
further toward awakening.

00:22:57.900 --> 00:23:01.320
The power to evolve humans and draw 
out the Evol powers within them...

00:23:01.320 --> 00:23:02.900
That is the power of the Queen.

00:23:06.200 --> 00:23:08.090
This is your final task.

00:23:08.090 --> 00:23:09.980
Fulfill it and you may gain a future

00:23:09.980 --> 00:23:11.960
where you live together with your sister.

00:23:21.870 --> 00:23:24.710
<i>My misunderstanding 
causes a missed meeting.</i>

00:23:24.710 --> 00:23:26.670
<i>In the season of colorful dancing leaves,</i>

00:23:27.150 --> 00:23:29.560
<i>a nostalgic melody is brought to mind.</i>

00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:31.030
<i>Episode five...</i>

00:23:31.030 --> 00:23:32.560
"An Amber Wind."

00:23:31.490 --> 00:23:34.970
"An Amber Wind"
